    {
      "id": "history_storage",
      "status": "partial",
      "summary": "Reactor now owns the UI-neutral history worker, reads the existing Store-compatible DPAPI v2 scan store off the UI thread, and renders live filtering, selection, refresh, and comparison summaries. Selecting the latest scan invalidates stale comparisons and identifies it as the baseline. Completed scans auto-save from the authoritative diagnostic session snapshot after the Store-matching cancellable 500 ms window, with explicit history-contract conversion and live retention/catalog providers; auto-save-off sends no request, retention-off acknowledges without a persistent scan, failures are nonfatal, and deterministic captures touch no storage. Detail/drill-down, tags and labels, trends, destructive clear confirmation, and the remaining loading/error/accessibility matrix remain unfinished.",
